research.recommendation:
1. Do not call M2M from the browser. CORS only allows *.usgs.gov, and the token must stay secret. Keep USGS_M2M_USERNAME and USGS_M2M_TOKEN (an app token scoped to 'M2M API') as GitHub Actions secrets. Run all M2M work in workflow_dispatch / repository_dispatch / cron Actions. The admin page can trigger them through the GitHub API with a fine-grained token held by the admin. If interactive search latency matters, a free Cloudflare Worker proxy is the fallback, since Firebase Functions need Blaze.

2. Harvest once, then refresh. The declass archive is closed (no new acquisitions), so a nightly or weekly Action can:
   - run scene-search over the city bbox for corona2, declassii and declassiii with metadataType=full;
   - store footprint, date, mission, camera, corners, Download Available and browse URLs in Firestore (or a static JSON);
   - copy the browse JPEGs into your own storage (they lack CORS), so the admin UI can draw footprints and previews with no live USGS calls.

3. In the admin UI, show for each frame: 'free – already scanned' (download-options available=true) or 'needs paid scan ($30 + $5 per order, 7/14 µm, about 3-4 weeks)'. Add a button that deep-links to EarthExplorer for that entityId. The user places and pays for the order manually; an agent must never handle payment.

4. A scheduled 'watch' Action polls download-options for entityIds the admin marked as ordered. When `available` flips to true, it runs: download → extract → mosaic segments → GCPs → gdalwarp → tile/COG → upload to Mapbox, then writes status back to Firestore.

5. Use usgsxplore (Python, maintained, MIT, login-token) as the M2M layer in the Action, or port the MIT Node scripts from Triavision-ai/historical-syria-explorer. Avoid landsatxplore, which still uses the removed password login. Use archive corners only for a first placement, and require GCP or human alignment before publishing. For street-level work, prefer KH-7 (declassii, camera H, about 0.6-1.2 m) or KH-9 panoramic (declassiii) over Corona or the KH-9 mapping camera.

6. Before building, confirm three things with the M2M role granted:
   - the dataset-search aliases;
   - the download-options productName/size for one scene per dataset;
   - whether order-products or order-submit work for declass (expect not).

research.concrete_details:
CDN imports (no bundler), pinned to one version:

```html
<script type="module">
import { initializeApp } from 'https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/13.0.0/firebase-app.js';
import { getAuth, GoogleAuthProvider, signInWithPopup, onAuthStateChanged } from 'https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/13.0.0/firebase-auth.js';
import { getFirestore, collection, query, where, orderBy, getDocs, addDoc, serverTimestamp, loadBundle, namedQuery, getDocsFromCache } from 'https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/13.0.0/firebase-firestore.js';
const app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig); // config is public by design
const auth = getAuth(app);
await signInWithPopup(auth, new GoogleAuthProvider()); // popup, NOT redirect, on github.io
</script>
```

- Keep authDomain as <project>.firebaseapp.com.
- Add `ventura8.github.io` (host only, no path or protocol) under Security > Authentication > Settings > Authorized domains.
- Use 12.19.0 instead if you would rather not ship a 4-day-old major version. The 13.0.0 breaking changes are AI Logic only.

firestore.rules (example):

```
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    function signedIn() { return request.auth != null; }
    function isAdmin() {
      return signedIn() && (request.auth.token.admin == true
        || exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/admins/$(request.auth.uid)));
    }
    function validPhoto(d) {
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['cityId','published','year','yearEnd','lat','lng','bearing','fov','title','caption','imageUrl','thumbUrl','source','license','createdAt','updatedAt','createdBy'])
        && d.keys().hasAll(['cityId','published','year','lat','lng','imageUrl'])
        && d.cityId is string && d.cityId.size() <= 64
        && d.published is bool
        && d.year is int && d.year >= 1800 && d.year <= 2100
        && d.lat is number && d.lat >= -90 && d.lat <= 90
        && d.lng is number && d.lng >= -180 && d.lng <= 180
        && (!('bearing' in d) || (d.bearing is number && d.bearing >= 0 && d.bearing < 360))
        && d.imageUrl is string && d.imageUrl.matches('^https://.*');
    }
    match /admins/{uid} { allow read: if signedIn() && request.auth.uid == uid; allow write: if false; } // create in console / Admin SDK
    match /cities/{cityId} { allow read: if resource.data.published == true || isAdmin(); allow write: if isAdmin(); }
    match /photos/{id} {
      allow read: if resource.data.published == true || isAdmin();
      allow create, update: if isAdmin() && validPhoto(request.resource.data);
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }
    match /layers/{id} { allow read: if resource.data.published == true || isAdmin(); allow write: if isAdmin(); }
  }
}
```

- The public client query must be `query(collection(db,'photos'), where('cityId','==','bucuresti'), where('published','==',true), orderBy('year'))`.
- The admin-only `/admins` documents are created by hand in the console. Console writes bypass rules.
- Each `exists()` costs one extra read per admin write.

firestore.indexes.json:

```json
{"indexes":[{"collectionGroup":"photos","queryScope":"COLLECTION","fields":[{"fieldPath":"cityId","order":"ASCENDING"},{"fieldPath":"published","order":"ASCENDING"},{"fieldPath":"year","order":"ASCENDING"}]}],"fieldOverrides":[]}
```

Add the same index for `layers` if it is queried the same way.

firebase.json:

```json
{"firestore":{"rules":"firestore.rules","indexes":"firestore.indexes.json"}}
```

Deploy:

```
npx firebase-tools@15 deploy --only firestore:rules,firestore:indexes --project <id> --non-interactive
```

GitHub Action outline (Node 22):

```yaml
- run: echo "$SA_KEY" > "$RUNNER_TEMP/sa.json"
  env: { SA_KEY: ${{ secrets.FIREBASE_SA_KEY }} }
- run: npx firebase-tools@15.33.0 deploy --only firestore --project $PID
  env: { GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS: ${{ runner.temp }}/sa.json }
```

- Python in the same job: `pip install firebase-admin==7.7.0`, then `import firebase_admin; from firebase_admin import firestore; firebase_admin.initialize_app(); db = firestore.client()` (ADC picks up GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS).
- Node in the same job: `firebase-admin@14.5.0` with `initializeApp({credential: applicationDefault()})`.
- Least-privilege SA roles (role IDs from memory, unverified): roles/datastore.user (data), roles/firebaserules.admin (rules), roles/datastore.indexAdmin (indexes), roles/serviceusage.serviceUsageConsumer.
- The default firebase-adminsdk-xxx key, from Project settings > Service accounts > Generate new private key, also works but has broader rights.
- WIF alternative: google-github-actions/auth@v3 with `permissions: {id-token: write, contents: read}` and `workload_identity_provider: projects/<num>/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/<pool>/providers/<prov>`. Add `service_account: ...` for impersonation (role roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser). Set the attribute condition `assertion.repository_owner == 'ventura8'`. Tokens last 5 to 10 minutes.

Console order (user does the steps marked *):
1. *Create the project and accept the Firebase terms. Turn Analytics off.
2. Add a web app (nickname) and copy the config.
3. Create Firestore: Databases & Storage > Firestore > Create database > Standard > location (eur3, europe-west3 or europe-central2; permanent) > production mode.
4. Enable Google: Security > Authentication > Sign-in method > Google > *choose project support email (usual console prompt; not confirmed in the current docs) > Save.
5. Under Settings > Authorized domains, add ventura8.github.io.
6. Project settings > Service accounts > Generate new private key, then store it as the GitHub secret FIREBASE_SA_KEY.
7. *Optional, only if billing is ever wanted: link a billing account (enter payment details) and set a budget alert.

Limits worth hard-coding as assumptions:
- Firestore: 50K reads, 20K writes and 20K deletes per day; 1 GiB stored; 10 GiB per month egress; 1 MiB per document; 200 composite indexes on Spark.
- Pages: 1 GB site, about 100 GB per month bandwidth.
- Repo: 100 MiB per file.
- Releases: assets under 2 GiB, at most 1000 per release.

Recommended storage pattern for ground photos on Spark:
- The admin page resizes in the browser with canvas to WebP: full size around 2048px (roughly 300-600 KB) and a thumbnail around 320px (roughly 20-40 KB).
- It commits both through the GitHub Contents API (PUT /repos/ventura8/<media-repo>/contents/photos/<id>.webp, base64 body, one request at a time) using a fine-grained PAT. The PAT is limited to Contents:write on that one repo and kept only in the admin's localStorage. Alternatively, the admin page sends a repository_dispatch to an Action.
- The site serves the photos through GitHub Pages of the media repo or jsDelivr gh URLs pinned to a commit.
- Raw purchased USGS scans go in GitHub Releases of a data repo, each under 2 GiB. Tiles go to Mapbox.
